# Local IPOs: a business of the city lists as a stock in the game. Lists the first candidate
# (rule lowered to one healthy day), checks the game has a stock for it at the offering price,
# closes the offering window and checks it trades, then has it bought out and checks the stock is
# gone. The city holds no shares, so no money moves; whatever is left is removed in cleanup and
# the building's Historical flag is put back as it was.
name local ipos: a company lists as a stock, opens its first day and is bought out
local-ipos on
ipo-healthy-days 1
ipo-scan
expect-ipo-candidates some
ipo-list-now
expect-log ipo: listed
expect-company offering listed
ipo-first-day
expect-log opened at
expect-company trading listed
show-economy
wait 1
capture ipo-listed
close-economy
ipo-buyout
expect-log was bought out at
expect-company gone unlisted
cleanup:
close-economy
ipo-remove-test
local-ipos restore
